                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### In Africa: Counting with Bones\n\nThe first counting system we know of arose in Africa about 37,000 years ago. It was inspired by our hands and was recorded with marks made on bones. Scholars such as Francisco A. González Redondo study these marks to understand when counting began.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
