               "text": "#### In Asia (Japan): The Soroban\n\nDuring the 16th century, according to the Gregorian calendar, the *suanpan* (算盤) reached Japan, where it became known as the *soroban* (算盤). This soroban is the closest approximation to the Roman *calculi* we saw earlier in this class.",
