         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nIn this class, we reviewed different numerical systems and observed that the time when they were created does not follow the path of human occupation of the world.\n\nAs a result, we can reach some conclusions:\n- We are all human, and knowledge did not arise in one place and then spread around the world.\n- The basis of mathematics was always everywhere.\n- We can reach the same conclusions by representing numbers in different ways.\n\nIn the next classes, we will learn how to work with these numbers.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
